WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
How many enablement people does your sales

2
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.420
plan need?

3
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.420
Here is a rule of thumb.

4
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.860
One enablement person for every 25 to

5
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.640
50 quota-carrying reps.

6
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.080
Count your reps.

7
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.060
Divide by 50, then by 25.

8
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.700
That is the range your plan assumes.

9
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.100
Now count the people you actually have.

10
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.700
If the plan assumes six and you

11
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.000
have two, the gap does not disappear.

12
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.720
It shows up somewhere else.

13
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.360
A kickoff with no follow-up, a launch

14
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.220
that reps learn from a slide deck,

15
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.920
new hires who ramp by shadowing whoever

16
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.580
has time.

17
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.980
The gap is not a judgment of

18
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:38.420
the team.

19
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:39.880
It is a planning error.

20
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.820
The work was sized, the hours were

21
00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.120
not.

22
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.540
Put both numbers on one page before

23
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.520
the plan is final.

24
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.540
Run yours in the free capacity calculator

25
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.260
at enablement.works
